    "summary_one_sentence": "United by a passion for drawing manga, overly confident Fujino and shut-in Kyomoto forge a deep, transformative friendship that shapes their artistic journeys and lives.",
    "summary_short": "In a small town, elementary student Fujino enjoys widespread praise for her 4-koma manga published in the school paper until the reclusive Kyomoto's superior artistic skills challenge her dominance. Driven by rivalry, Fujino works tirelessly to improve, eventually meeting Kyomoto and discovering that the shut-in is actually her biggest fan. Joining forces as a creative duo, they collaborate on successful manga projects while navigating the awkwardness and beauty of growing up together. However, as their paths begin to diverge toward adulthood, a tragic turn of events forces Fujino to reflect on the true power and weight of their shared artistic connection.",
    "summary_long": "Fujino is a talented fifth-grader whose 4-panel manga strips in the school newspaper earn her praise from classmates and teachers alike. Her self-assurance is shaken when the school principal asks her to share her layout space with Kyomoto, a severely social-anxious classmate who refuses to attend school. Kyomoto's submitted artwork displays a stunning, detailed mastery of background art that instantly eclipses Fujino's simple comic style. Humiliated yet determined not to be outdone, Fujino devotes all her free time to practicing visual drawing, only to give up after years of realizing the gap remains vast. Upon graduating middle school, Fujino is tasked with delivering Kyomoto's diploma, leading to an unexpected meeting where Kyomoto passionately confesses her long-time admiration for Fujino's comics. Reignited by this validation, Fujino invites Kyomoto out of isolation, and the two form a creative partnership submitting one-shot manga under a shared pseudonym. Their work garners critical acclaim and serial publication offers, but Kyomoto ultimately chooses to pursue formal art education at a university rather than remain Fujino's assistant. When a sudden, senseless tragedy strikes the art campus, Fujino is crushed by grief and burdened by guilt over bringing Kyomoto out into the world. Through an emotional journey involving a magical alternate reality where they never met, Fujino comes to realize that creating art was always their ultimate form of connection, inspiring her to keep drawing in honor of their bond.",
    "synopsis": "Look Back is an intimate, emotionally resonant story exploring the creative impulse, the solitude of art making, and the powerful bond forged between two young girls. Fujino is a confident, outgoing elementary student who thrives on the admiration her short manga strips receive from her peers. Her artistic world shifts when she meets Kyomoto, a room-bound recluse whose intricate background illustrations reveal a breathtaking artistic talent. What begins as a silent competition evolves into a profound partnership as the two join forces to create comics together, drawing each other out of their respective comfort zones. As time pushes them toward different choices regarding their futures, the story delicately examines friendship, tragedy, grief, and the enduring passion that drives creators to keep telling stories even when faced with overwhelming loss.",
